                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/1524: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        Chungking</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-10T17:00:00-04:00">August 10, 1938—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>227. Your 400, August 7, noon, in regard to automobile and bicycle license fees
                    at Chefoo. The Department concurs in the opinion of the Embassy that the license
                    fees in question do not appear to be unreasonable and that, provided the fees
                    are collected from foreigners and Chinese without discrimination and the funds
                    so collected are used for road repairs, American nationals should be advised to
                    pay the fees as voluntary contributions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
